                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A sesamoid bone or sesamoid cartilage."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7c5ac420-f14a-45a0-90fa-1fc25ebb2bc6",
                                                "sense_id": "0ab8202d-8d29-3937-92e2-d19150d71572",
                                                "text": "There are also at least two examples of more complex ectopic digits. The first is in the aye-aye, a Madagascan lemur, which has a distinct pseudothumb on its forelimb consisting of a bony part that is an expanded radial sesamoid and a dense cartilaginous extension (Hartstone-Rose et al., 2019)."
                                            }
                                        ]
